Subject: [PATCH] nexmon: define SDIO_DEVICE_ID_BROADCOM_CYPRESS_43752 for 6.12.115

Local compatibility patch for this project (packages/espnow-nexmon), not
upstream. Linux 6.12.115 renamed the SDIO id SDIO_DEVICE_ID_BROADCOM_CYPRESS_43752
to SDIO_DEVICE_ID_BROADCOM_43752 (include/linux/mmc/sdio_ids.h, value 0xaae8,
unchanged). Kali's driver still uses the old name in bcmsdh.c and sdio.c, so
it fails to compile. This only adds the old name as an alias when the kernel
does not define it. The device-table entries and the value are unchanged.
The value 0xaae8 matches the upstream v6.12 sdio_ids.h.

--- a/brcmfmac-nexmon-dkms-fff319040f6a8034fce36f846cce2dc19de1b396/include/brcm_hw_ids.h
+++ b/brcmfmac-nexmon-dkms-fff319040f6a8034fce36f846cce2dc19de1b396/include/brcm_hw_ids.h
@@ -9,6 +9,10 @@
 #include <linux/pci_ids.h>
 #include <linux/mmc/sdio_ids.h>
 
+#ifndef SDIO_DEVICE_ID_BROADCOM_CYPRESS_43752
+#define SDIO_DEVICE_ID_BROADCOM_CYPRESS_43752	0xaae8
+#endif
+
 #define BRCM_USB_VENDOR_ID_BROADCOM	0x0a5c
 #define BRCM_USB_VENDOR_ID_LG		0x043e
 #define BRCM_USB_VENDOR_ID_LINKSYS	0x13b1
